**Read:** [Chemical Reactor Analysis and Design Fundamentals — Rawlings and Ekerdt](../sources/Chemical-Reactor-Analysis-Rawlings-Ekerdt.lingua#r_7YQAV27Y3J0B537Z6K5HDN8H0A), the entire heterogeneous-reaction, transport-limitation and scale-related material; [Chemical and Biological Reaction Engineering — MIT 10.37](../sources/Reaction-Engineering-MIT-10-37.lingua#r_67AEXD9K1DJ46SV942PAZHZ4BZ), the complete diffusion/heat-transfer and catalysis assignments; [Chemical Technology: From Principles to Products — Jess and Wasserscheid](../sources/Chemical-Technology-Jess-Wasserscheid.lingua#r_38DBBMW0BMR89K3R95V073YA41), the full transport-limitation criteria and heterogeneous-kinetics treatment if using this commercial route.

An intrinsic chemical rate uses the local state at the reacting site. A measured vessel or catalyst-particle rate can instead depend on delivery of reactants, removal of products and heat, and the distribution of accessible material. External films, pores, interfaces and bulk mixing introduce distinct resistances and time scales.

Compare reaction, diffusion, convection and heat-removal scales with compatible definitions. A ratio such as a Damköhler number only has meaning after its characteristic reaction and transport scales are stated. Reducing particle size or changing agitation can test a suspected limitation, but may also change other properties and must be interpreted with actual evidence.

Geometric scaling changes area/volume, flow patterns, thermal paths and residence histories. Preserving one dimensionless group rarely preserves every relevant mechanism. Extrapolating a small well-mixed experiment to a large multiphase reactor therefore needs a hierarchy of models and independent observations.

**Work:** reconstruct a complete published reaction/transport study, derive the limiting cases and test an alternative explanation for an apparent rate. Design observations that distinguish intrinsic kinetics, external transfer, internal diffusion and thermal influences. Compare the implications for catalyst form, equipment and operation without treating a model correlation as verified plant behavior.

**Continue:** [Infer residence histories and test whether an ideal reactor model fits the evidence](Residence-time-distributions-bypass-and-mixing-models.lingua#r_54MXGD8AKQ76G6PEC1MC2WPWY1).

**Return:** [Industrial chemistry — chemical transformations, useful products and continuing production](../Industrial-chemistry.lingua#r_3AKBAFB2ABJ0671QW6ZBQ0B618).
